From: BearddOddity <saintlyendless@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:31:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] Add a mod API: client-side modules written against one
 small, stable interface

A module is a folder (module.json + one ES module) that names itself, the
interface it was written for and every event it listens to, as a crate names
its edition and dependencies. It never names a game build; the interface is
append-only, so a module for interface N runs on every game with N or more.
Client-side only: the bus carries nothing to the server and changes no wire.

- src/mods/modApi.js: the manifest, the version law, the event table
  (questMark, quests, drawFx), the bus and a module's frozen handle
- src/mods/moduleHost.js: read, judge and start each installed module; a bad
  one is a line in the report, one that is off is never imported
- src/mods/modBus.js, src/main.js: the game's one bus; modules started off
  the entry's static graph, where a desktop shell offers a Mods folder
- app/lib/moduleFiles.cjs, app/preload.cjs: the Mods folder read for the
  page - a plain slug and a plain .js name, nothing past them
- src/ui/enhancedHud.js, scenes/hostMagic.js, scenes/questBridge.js: the
  three events announced at their seams
- src/ui/modulesCard.js, settingsMap.js: Settings > Mods & files > Modules,
  a switch per module
- modules/: three modules written against it (quest waypoint, quest panel,
  guide trail of gold embers) and scripts/buildModules.mjs
- test/mods1_api.test.js; bible: Mod-API page, Ledger A row, the pins the
  new card and files move, and 25 languages' machine drafts of the card

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
