UN and the picture is how it was caught: the panels photographed 46px off the right edge with a live transform, because NOTICE_WATCHDOG_MS had correctly swept a panel nobody was drawing - a harness that does not do what the host does measures its own artefact, so it PUMPS the draw on rAF the way a host does. 12 measurements, 3 shots. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `npm run blood` (tools/bloodProbe.mjs) drives `createHitEffects` and `drawBillboards` over a texture whose colour is known, in a real WebGL2 context, and reads the pixel back at five lighting states. MAC-BUG W6: and then installs the Enhanced Lighting lane and reads a sprite and a mark side by side at four more - the rows where the mark came back at 25 against 69 and 2 against 17 while every classic row was green. 26 checks (AUDIT BLOOD3 F10: and the MENISCUS is drawn now - the same mark against a uniform-thickness one under a grazing sun, the difference banded by radius, which is the one law this arc took to main with no picture; the film's own rows, banded by RADIUS inside the mark's silhouette rather than by brightness, which was sorting the alpha-faded rim into the thin bucket and measuring the blend). It exists because MAC-BUG W4 ("Also blood is black") could not be settled by reading: it clears the pool, the texture KEY (`380_0#0` is minted in scenes/dataPipeline.js and asked for in render/renderer.js, and nothing had ever checked the two agree), the shader's emission arm, and anything specific to blood - a plain sprite in the same dungeon light comes back the same 20,2,2. 9 checks. PROBE (no suite row - it needs a browser): `node tools/setUiProbe.mjs` draws the REAL pack (`createInventoryWindow`, the enhanced skin) and the REAL HUD with a kit worn through the game's own equip - six of Dagon's Brand and its sword, two of Ruhn's Regalia, a Mora helm and a Nocturnal cuirass carried - online at Renown 12, at a desktop, a laptop and a phone: the doll's strip (two lines, "7/9" and "2/9", their