ll, DFU's specialInfection exception is exempt, and the monster-hit path still DRAWS both rolls for an immune target because FormulaHelper.InflictDisease (:1689-1712) carries no immunity test at all. F16 THE SILENCE LANDING ALERT: Silence.cs:80-96's printer, the second of DFU's two and the one the port lacked - a landing on the player says 'You are silenced.' exactly once, a renewing recast says nothing further and still renews its rounds (STACK-CAP) (EntityEffectManager.cs:553-558 refuses the unflagged incumbent, so DoConstantEffects never ticks it), a foe's silence lands mute because the foe sink sets carry no `say` at all - the port's rendering of `manager.EntityBehaviour == PlayerEntityBehaviour` - and the cast-time gate's SILENCED_TEXT re-points at the same literal so the two printers cannot drift. F17's pins live in x11b.test.js, where the defect's guard stood. |
 | audit64_time_weather.test.js | 15 | AUDIT 64 (2026-09-08), the WORLD TIME AND WEATHER lane - three laws about what a town does with the clock, each red under the mutation that reverts it. **F8 THE GLASS BURNED ON THE WRONG FLAG.** Both writers of a window style in DFU read `IsCityLightsOn`: DaggerfallLocation.ApplyTimeAndSpace (Internal/DaggerfallLocation.cs:141-145, re-run off the :120-129 poll keyed on `lastCityLightsFlag != Now.IsCityLightsOn`) and DayNight.Set (Utility/AssetInjection/Components/DayNight.cs:90 -> :120); nothing anywhere reads IsNight for one. IsCityLightsOn is hour >= 17 || hour < 8 and IsNight is hour < 6 || hour >= 18 (Utility/DaggerfallDateTime.cs:155-157, :171-173 over the constants at :48-51), so the port's town windows lit an hour late and unlit two hours early beside lanterns it already read correctly. Pinned at the four hours where the two properties disagree, across both disagreeing hour-windows, and swept over all 1440 minutes as one flag with two halves - with the day/night emission rows (MaterialReader.cs:111-118) pinned beside them so the law is visible rather than nominal. **F9 THE FOG STYLE HAD NO ASSIGNER.** WindowStyle.Fog is declared (DaggerfallUnityEnums.cs:87-94) and spent (MaterialReader.cs:927-929 over FogWindowColor :113 / FogWindowIntensity :117) but ASSIGNED by nothing - the tree's writers are DaggerfallLocation.cs:44/:143/:145, DayNight.cs:120, DaggerfallInterior.cs:473/:517/:1270 and DaggerfallBankPurchasePopUp.cs:267, and Game/WeatherManager.cs does not contain the word - yet the port let a fog roll override the clock at both exterior hosts, ungated and with no Ledger row. Pinned as an absence: weather.js exports no window-style rule at all, and both hosts' setWindowEmission line reads the `?window=` dev override then `windowStyleForTime(minute)` with nothing between. The WINDOW_STYLES.fog ROW is pinned KEPT beside `custom` - verbatim MaterialReader data, still reachable through ?window=fog, exactly the standing DFU leaves it. **F10 THE FESTIVAL PARCHMENT.** PlayerEnterExit.ShowHolidayText (Game/PlayerEnterExit.cs:565-585) had no port: record 8349 + GetHolidayId, ClickAnywhereToClose. Pinned as the three-part member it is - the id arithmetic and its zero on an ordinary day; the type gate over all fifteen LOCATION_TYPES, since DFU primes only on the town arm (:1382-1383) and a dungeon or graveyard takes the flavour-text arm (:1364-1367) while Coven and HomeYourShips fall out of both; the 2.5 s prime (:1406); the cancel when the remembered location object is no longer current (:355-359); the DEFERRAL under an open window rather than a drop, since IsPlayerOnHUD (:364, GameManager.cs:400-403) leaves the timer at zero and primed true; and the ten-second re-arm set on a NON-holiday entry, because :584 sits OUTSIDE the `if (holidayId != 0)` block - the mutation that folds it in is red. **REVIEW ROUND (2026-09-08): the host pins held SHAPE, not ARGUMENT.** The four fragments named no argument, and both arguments that decide whether the feature works survived a fully green suite: `enterLocationRect(_musicLoc)` -> `enterLocationRect({})` (the :355 identity cancel then fires on the next frame and the box can never appear anywhere) and `regionIndex: () => _questRegionIndex()` -> `() => 0` (a regional holiday announced in the wrong province, FormulaHelper.cs:1841). The pins are now a WINDOW over each host's `_holidayText.update(dt, { … });` block: the expression its `currentLocation` thunk returns is extracted from the source and the prime is REQUIRED to pass that same expression, the `regionIndex` term to be the host's own CurrentRegionIndex idiom (`_questRegionIndex()` / `dfLocation.regionIndex`), the clock term classic minutes (:569), the HUD term the deferring `!gamePaused()` (:364). Beside them a BEHAVIOURAL region pin - Scour Day (row 1, region byte 0x19 = region INDEX 24, day 2) fires in region 24 and is silent in every other, through `holidayTextId` and through a full prime-and-drain, re-arm set either way. And the lane's recorded departure from BOTH verifiers is pinned at last: the drain sits ABOVE the modal gate because PlayerEnterExit.Update (:325, block :355-368) has no isPlayerInside guard and IsPlayerOnHUD (GameManager.cs:400-402 -> IsHUDTopWindow :915) is a UI-window test - a source-offset comparison in both hosts fails if it sinks into the exterior-only path, where `modes.frame` returning true would suspend it for exactly the case DFU keeps running. 18 mutations, 18 dead |
